Adjacency matrix representation.

Adjacency matrix is an 2 dimensional array that indicates which edges the graph contains. 
We can check if there is an edge between 2 nodes. -> if yes -> 1 , if not -> 0

int adj[N][N];

(1) -> (2) -> (3)
 ^      |      /
  \     |     /
   \    V    V
    (   4   )


    1 2  3 4
1   |0|1|0|0|
    --------
2   |0|0|1|1|
    --------
3   |0|0|0|1|
    ---------
4   |1|0|0|0|

(1) -[5]-> (2) -[7]-> (3)
 ^         |           /
[2]        |[6]       /[5]
   \       V         V
    (      4         )

    1 2  3 4
1   |0|5|0|0|
    --------
2   |0|0|7|6|
    --------
3   |0|0|0|5|
    ---------
4   |2|0|0|0|

adj[a][b] : length of edge from node a to node b.

Drawback of adjacency matrix is most of them is zero -> the representation cannot be used if the graph is large.

